@startuml
title CU-D8 - Exclusion atomica de doble reserva (invariante de CU-D7)
autonumber
participant "CU-D7 / transaccion A" as TxA
participant "CU-D7 / transaccion B" as TxB
participant "AvailabilitySlotReservationService\n+ implementacion Agenda" as Reservation
participant AvailabilitySlotRepository as SlotRepository
database PostgreSQL as DB

note over TxA,TxB
  Intercalacion ilustrativa con A ganadora.
  No es una nueva operacion de usuario ni un endpoint propio.
end note

TxA -> Reservation: reserveUsableSlot(mismo slotId)
Reservation -> SlotRepository: reserveUsableSlot(slotId), A
SlotRepository -> DB: UPDATE condicional A\nstatus = AVAILABLE AND schedule.active
DB --> SlotRepository: 1 fila; bloqueo hasta fin de TxA
SlotRepository --> Reservation: 1
Reservation -> SlotRepository: findByIdWithSchedule(slotId)
SlotRepository -> DB: SELECT slot + schedule
DB --> SlotRepository: slot y schedule
SlotRepository --> Reservation: AvailabilitySlot
Reservation --> TxA: AvailabilitySlotReference
TxB -> Reservation: reserveUsableSlot(mismo slotId)
Reservation -> SlotRepository: reserveUsableSlot(slotId), B
SlotRepository -> DB: UPDATE condicional B sobre misma fila
note right of DB
  B puede esperar por la fila de A.
  El test actual no mide esa espera.
end note
TxA -> DB: INSERT cita SCHEDULED
TxA -> DB: COMMIT
DB --> SlotRepository: B reevalua condicion; 0 filas
SlotRepository --> Reservation: 0
Reservation --> TxB: SlotReservationRejectedException
note right of TxB: CU-D7 traduce a 409 SLOT_UNAVAILABLE

note over Reservation,DB
  V3: uq_appointments_active_slot protege unicidad de
  citas SCHEDULED/CONFIRMED por slot_id.
  No se usa PESSIMISTIC_WRITE en la creacion actual.
end note
@enduml
